From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: decode Dolby Vision profiles 5, 7 and 8 natively

HEVC streams whose container record (AV_PKT_DATA_DOVI_CONF in the codec
context's coded side data, at least as large as the public struct) has
both an RPU and a base layer are decoded with VideoToolbox's Dolby Vision
HEVC decoder ('dvh1') instead of a plain HEVC session:

- profiles 5 and 8 natively; profile 7 as profile 8.1, with a rewritten
  configuration record, every RPU converted by libdovi 3.3.2 (mode 2) and
  no enhancement layer;
- the decoder specification keeps pristine's hvcC atom and the
  Enable-hardware key, and adds a 24-byte DOVIDecoderConfigurationRecord
  as dvvC (profile 8 and converted 7) or dvcC (profile 5), with the
  metadata compression and reserved bits always zero; for an HDR
  base (profiles 7 and 8) it also carries BT.2020 primaries, PQ (HLG for
  profile 8 with compatibility id 4) and the BT.2020 matrix;
- if VideoToolbox refuses the session and the base is HDR, one more
  attempt is made with a plain HEVC description; profile 5 never retries;
- a Dolby Vision session asks for per-frame HDR display metadata where the
  OS has the properties, ignoring (and logging at verbose) a failure;
- at the end of each frame every type 62 NAL unit of the packet longer
  than 2 bytes is appended after the slices, unchanged for profiles 5 and
  8 or converted for profile 7. An RPU that cannot be converted or
  appended is left out with warnings and the frame is still decoded.
  Profile 7 RPUs that are empty once their header, emulation prevention
  bytes and trailing zero bytes are removed are skipped without calling
  libdovi, because libdovi 3.3.2 aborts the process on them. For profile
  7 streams, RPU and enhancement layer NAL units never reach the sample
  any other way;
- decoded buffers from a Dolby Vision session keep VideoToolbox's own
  attachments (DolbyVisionRPUData among them) instead of FFmpeg's, and for
  an HDR base get BT.2020, PQ or HLG and a colour space only where
  missing. The decision follows the session current when the frame is
  output, through a reference each frame holds.

Every other stream and codec is decoded as before. The Dolby Vision logic
lives in its own file, videotoolbox_dovi.c. libavcodec now references
libdovi's C API; FFmpeg's configure has no switch for it, so the build
passes libdovi's include path and -ldovi through its compiler and linker
flags. Applies to FFmpeg n8.0.1 on top of Vivid's patches 0001 to 0010.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for
FFmpeg. Like the files it modifies, it is free software; you can
redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser
